Keep offset 0 valid when interior pointers are switched after GC_init.

GC_init resets the valid offsets and then registers offset 0, so a
pointer to the start of an object counts (misc.c:1364-1365). The
setter resets them the same way and does not register offset 0 again.
gc.h allows the late call: "if the GC is already initialized, the
setter acquires the GC lock".

huggorm calls GC_INIT at import and nix::initGC at the first
evaluator, so that importing starts no marker thread. nix::initGC
calls GC_set_all_interior_pointers(0), and without offset 0 the
collector freed `builtins` under a live evaluator: "attribute 'length'
missing", then a segfault (huggorm tasks/101).

bdwgc master (2026-09-28) has the same code.

--- a/misc.c
+++ b/misc.c
@@ -2575,6 +2575,7 @@
       /* even after switching the mode.                                 */
       LOCK();
       GC_initialize_offsets(); /* NOTE: this resets manual offsets as well */
+      GC_register_displacement_inner(0L); /* as GC_init does */
       if (!GC_all_interior_pointers)
         GC_bl_init_no_interiors();
       UNLOCK();
